 ## Overview
-BasicDAGColorsBase is the foundational class for managing color data within the BasicDAG sparse voxel structure. It solves the problem of memory fragmentation and traversal inefficiency by decoupling leaf color storage from the main geometry array. It differs from its sibling [BasicDAGUncompressedColors](6741-basicdaguncompressedcolors.md) by enforcing a specific memory layout strategy where leaf counts are stored in a dedicated, enclosed array, ensuring the core DAG structure remains compact and uniform for fast traversal [S1, unofficial].
+BasicDAGColorsBase is a base class for managing color data within a Sparse Voxel DAG structure. It solves the problem of decoupling leaf count storage from the main geometry array by utilizing an enclosed leaves array. This separation allows for more flexible memory management and traversal strategies compared to tightly coupled geometry-color representations. It differs from its siblings, [BasicDAGUncompressedColors](6741-basicdaguncompressedcolors.md) and [Mixture Graph](11065-mixture-graph.md), by providing the foundational storage mechanism for leaf counts without implementing specific compression or mixture logic itself.
 
 ## Shared principles
-The family shares a specific memory layout strategy where leaf counts are stored in a dedicated, enclosed array rather than interleaved with the DAG node indices. This design ensures that the core DAG structure, which stores node indices in a flat array for fast traversal, remains compact and uniform.
